piano-sensors (4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Import the odm JSON sensor configuration again, and link
    /odm/etc/sensors/config to it: after every ADSP start the sensors PD
    reads json.lst first and gives up without it, even with a valid
    registry on persist. Version 3 only worked on an ADSP that had already
    read its configuration.

 -- piano mainline contributors <piano@localhost>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0800

piano-sensors (3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Serve the sensors PD with adsprpcd (Qualcomm FastRPC, Debian
    fastrpc-support) instead of a patched hexagonrpcd: it implements the
    remote file calls the PD makes, and opens its paths as they are.
  * With a valid registry on persist the PD does not read the odm JSON
    configuration: import persist only, drop the super/odm import.
  * Override fastrpc-support's udev rule that starts every remote
    processor, and mask its root PD and audio PD daemons.

 -- piano mainline contributors <piano@localhost>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:30:00 +0800

piano-sensors (2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Read odm_a from the super partition: it is a dynamic partition with
    no partition label of its own, so the import waited for it forever.
  * Do not order the import after block device units, and drop the
    xiaomi,piano firmware condition: ABL boots the stock tree, whose
    compatible is qcom,sun.
  * Conflict with droid-juicer, which hexagonrpcd recommends: it spins
    on piano and holds the display manager back.

 -- piano mainline contributors <piano@localhost>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:50:00 +0800

piano-sensors (1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: sensors PD inputs imported from the device's own
    partitions, hexagonrpcd and iio-sensor-proxy set up for piano.

